  "independent_findings": [
    {
      "topic": "Original entry and borrowed storage",
      "finding": "Selected UseUserBuffer preserves actual brand CHECK, Buffer::Data then Length, uv_buf_init(unsigned int), native allocation and listener publication. The listener owns only its native Listener record and uv_buf_t, with no JS root or backing entitlement. The caller must keep the already-backed view/storage alive and valid through I/O.",
      "evidence": [
        "source-map:original_use",
        "source-map:original_buffer_brand_data_length",
        "source-map:original_inheritance_storage_delete",
        "source-map:selected_buffer_and_use"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Allocation and retirement",
      "finding": "The native ABI declares DiagnosticContextScope first, then scopes the actual memory domain. The accepted standard allocator retries the real new_handler and reaches native nonreturning bad_alloc policy rather than a nullable or JS allocation result. The max-aligned native allocation prefix retains the independent memory owner on successful allocation and releases charge/domain after storage free; an already unlinked listener can therefore retire after Engine teardown with null diagnostic context.",
      "evidence": [
        "source-map:selected_native_allocation",
        "source-map:original_standard_new",
        "source-map:native_bad_alloc_policy",
        "source-map:host_allocation_prefix_complete",
        "source-map:host_domain_refcount_charge",
        "source-map:host_engine_release"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Read branches and replacement order",
      "finding": "OnAllocate returns the stored buffer and ignores suggestion. Null-base negative reads take the normal read check and ignore callback replacement. Other reads CHECK base identity and use skip-nread-checks; they do not compare incoming length. Only a present nonundefined result replaces base and then native len, preserving the Windows ULONG versus Unix size_t distinction. Initial uv_buf_init still narrows through unsigned int.",
      "evidence": [
        "source-map:original_custom_read",
        "source-map:selected_read_body",
        "source-map:original_uv_init_body",
        "source-map:original_uv_win_width",
        "source-map:original_uv_unix_width"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Self-destruction and completion",
      "finding": "After callback on empty/undefined or null-negative paths, the selected owner uses only retained local Environment/Scope state, not the potentially destroyed listener or stream. Nonundefined replacement retains the original requirement that the listener remain alive. Ordinary/uncatchable failure is handled through the existing real operation Scope; arbitrary Engine destruction during the callback is not admitted.",
      "evidence": [
        "source-map:selected_destroy_alloc_read_scope",
        "source-map:selected_escaping_completion",
        "source-map:host_call_js",
        "source-map:host_scope_pending_own",
        "source-map:host_scope_finish"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Unlink and reporter",
      "finding": "The actual listener destructor unlinks before freeing native storage. Resource destruction tolerates self-removal using the preserved pointer comparison. after_shutdown selects the genuine reusable shutdown.reportAfterShutdown, not a previous-listener forwarding substitute. Full write-request reporting remains outside the unit.",
      "evidence": [
        "source-map:original_resource_destructor_remove",
        "source-map:host_emit_and_chain_teardown",
        "source-map:selected_destroy_alloc_read_scope",
        "source-map:host_actual_shutdown_reporter"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "VM boundary",
      "finding": "Actual QuickJS typed-array/DataView predicates and raw view intrinsics are used without guest getters, allocation, backing acquisition or pending-state mutation. Detached, out-of-bounds or zero-length observations do not grant permission to dereference memory. Original V8 on-heap GetBuffer materialization/fatal allocation is explicitly excluded.",
      "evidence": [
        "source-map:original_getbuffer_materialization",
        "source-map:original_view_offset_length",
        "source-map:host_raw_view_data_length"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Controls",
      "finding": "All fifteen full control bodies were read and remain byte-identical to A252. They cover borrowed physical storage, DataView shadow getters, zero/negative/read replacement paths, actual descriptor reads, ordinary and uncatchable reasons, external backing non-retention, head/interior unlink, self-deleting chains, unlinked post-Engine retirement, callback destruction and the actual Shutdown reporter. They are source controls with no execution claim.",
      "evidence": [
        "source-map:control_01 through control_15",
        "selected control A25266B2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "topic": "Current build composition",
      "finding": "The selected block links the already present node_one_byte_diagnostics once and directly compiles only allocation.cpp. Network links the sole native_node_memory owner. The shared diagnostic library supplies TLS C, V8 fatal C++ and OneByteString diagnostics C++ once for this selected artifact. addTest has the existing default cache name and explicit install destination, with no run step. No duplicate member or altered old build bytes found.",
      "evidence": [
        "composition:current_build_insertion",
        "composition:historical_install_block_adaptation",
        "source-map:host_network_recipe",
        "source-map:host_memory_recipe",
        "source-map:host_shared_diagnostic_library",
        "source-map:selected_install_block"
      ]
    }
  ],
